# Import Alias Rules

Keep imports stable and prevent boundary drift.

## Root aliases
From `jsconfig.json`:
- `@app/* -> src/app/*`
- `@lib/* -> src/lib/*`
- `@middlewares/* -> src/middlewares/*`
- `@config/* -> src/config/*`
- `@prisma/client -> src/prisma/client.js`
- `@logs/* -> logs/*`
- `@websockets/* -> src/websockets/*`
- `@modules/* -> src/modules/*`

## Module aliases
- `@controllers/<module>`, `@services/<module>`, `@repositories/<module>`, `@validations/<module>`, `@routes/<module>`

## Requirements
- Use aliases for cross-folder imports; relative imports stay within the same folder tree only.
- Modules may import another module only through public service or shared-lib entrypoints.
- Controllers and repositories must not be imported across modules.
- Alias changes require synchronized updates to runtime alias registration and docs.
- Imports must not create circular dependency chains.
